3. Academic Papers & Architectural Inspirations (Clean-Room Implementations)
   学术论文与架构思想参考（独立净室实现，未复用任何原论文代码）
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Several cognitive algorithms in `src/core/` were independently designed and
implemented in clean-room JavaScript inspired by published research:

  * HippoRAG — Gutiérrez et al. (2024), "HippoRAG: Neurobiologically Inspired
    Long-Term Memory for Large Language Models" (arXiv:2405.14831)
    -> Inspired Personalized PageRank (PPR) multi-hop associative traversal in
       `src/core/memory-graph-v2.mjs`.

  * Zep / Graphiti — Rasmussen et al. (2025), "Zep: A Temporal Knowledge Graph
    Architecture for Agent Memory" (arXiv:2501.13956)
    -> Inspired bi-temporal validity windows (`valid_at` / `invalid_at`) and
       polarity supersession preserving historical taste changes in
       `src/core/memory-graph-v2.mjs`.

  * MemGPT / Letta & Sleep-Time Compute — Packer et al. (2023, arXiv:2310.08560);
    Lin et al. (2025, "Sleep-time Compute: Beyond Inference Scaling at Test-time")
    -> Inspired off-peak sleep-time episodic consolidation and compact core
       memory capsules in `src/core/episode-consolidation.mjs` and
       `src/core/sleep-dream.mjs`.

  * PAD Emotional State Model — Mehrabian & Russell (1974), "An Approach to
    Environmental Psychology"
    -> Inspired continuous 3D Pleasure-Arousal-Dominance affective inertia and
       homeostatic decay in `src/core/emotion-pad.mjs`.

  * Generative Agents — Park et al. (2023), "Generative Agents: Interactive
    Simulacra of Human Behavior" (arXiv:2304.03442)
    -> Inspired hierarchical memory reflection and daily circadian rhythm
       design in `src/core/growth-evolution.mjs` and `src/core/inner-life.mjs`.


